    <string name="give_own_space_title">Give %s its own space?</string>
    <string name="give_own_space_confirm">Give it its space</string>
    <string name="own_space_explanation">To keep passwords, %s moves into a space of its own on the server: it can no longer read the other agents, nor they its own, and its tools work in a sandbox when the server allows it. Its conversations, memory and routines go with it. About 30 seconds.</string>
    <string name="own_space_help_isolated">%s has a space of its own: it can use credentials from the vault, and the other agents can\'t read its files.</string>
    <string name="own_space_help_shared">%s shares the server with the other agents created here. For it to use credentials from the vault, give it its own space.</string>
    <string name="delete_agent">Delete %s</string>
    <string name="delete_agent_title">Delete %s?</string>
    <string name="delete_agent_body">Its conversations, memory and routines are erased from the server. This can\'t be undone.</string>
    <string name="delete_agent_help">Its conversations, memory and routines are erased from the server.</string>
    <string name="give_tool">Give « %1$s » to %2$s?</string>
    <string name="give_tool_protected">%s will be able to act on the server it runs on, which it shares with the other agents created here. Don\'t trust it with passwords: agents that keep some will soon get their own space.</string>
    <string name="give_tool_unprotected">This server doesn\'t isolate its agents: %s will be able to read the server\'s keys and use them to command your other agents. Only turn this on if you trust everything it reads (web pages, e-mails, documents).</string>
